        "title": "Plant Defenses - Alkaloids, Terpenes, Phenolics, and the Arms Race",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Plants cannot run away. Their defense system is entirely chemical — a library of ~200,000 known secondary metabolites evolved specifically to deter, damage, or manipulate herbivores, pathogens, and competitors. These same compounds are why food is flavorful, why medicine works, and why some plants are toxic."
    },
